# iterative thinking — what the click would refuse is not retried: the button is offered, the click refuses
#
# The wolf in the Test Den is an enemy in the same area, so UnderThreatImpossibleRule refuses any act
# that is not about facing it (unless the means is discreet). That is an action rule, the click's: a
# thinking retries only what is refused before the click (the willingness and choice rules), so even
# with a retry left (--doubt medium) "examine the wolf" is offered as a button, and clicking it gives
# the threat's refusal.
#
# Woodcraft is pinned as the means (it observes, and is not discreet).
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Den" --period noon --observe-only wolf --grant-mm woodcraft --means-only woodcraft --doubt medium

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

strategy succeed
goal examine
# The beast confronts whoever walks in, and so is on the map already observed.
click think "wolf"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
expect-no-state texts "That will not do, and I think again"
expect-state trees means=woodcraft
regions

click act 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
expect-state texts "while under the threat of"
quit
